king. One exception covers the JavaScript-off rendering only: a declared non-default state reachable only by script, declared `requiresScript: true` with its trigger recorded, resolves on the scripted rendering alone (same element, AA and review conditions); the default state always needs both renderings, and a `requiresScript` claim on a state that renders with JavaScript off (every text the scripted rendering shows is shown without script, compared by text rather than element position) fails as an integrity mismatch. For a valid claim the JavaScript-off baseline is the default state's JavaScript-off rendering, and content present only in the scripted state passes only as approved copy slots placed in that state. A script-only state may replace a default slot (search results replacing the page description) only when the copy deck places the new slot in that state and does not place the old one there; a replaced slot that is still placed in the state, and any change to copy both renderings show, stay INCOMPLETE. The `requiresScript` check compares counted word tokens, so splitting a text run into inline elements does not change it.
 
