+| R20-MIMAR-01 | PARTIAL | [width-screen.mjs:225](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:225) rejects wholly lost or partly clipped content at another width. Inspected regression [panel-r20.test.mjs:77](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tests/panel-r20.test.mjs:77) checks the table and LTR/RTL nav, with failing assertions at `:95`; the old inline-end exemption would fail these expectations. Content hidden by responsive CSS escapes the comparison: R21-GPT-04. Browser regression not rerun. |
+
+| ID | Part | Severity | file:line | Evidence | Exact fix |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| R21-GPT-01 | A | P2 | [width-screen.mjs:19](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:19), [width-screen.mjs:38](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:38), [width-screen.mjs:98](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:98) | **Yes, the rule applies to images/media.** `MEDIA` includes `img, svg, video, canvas`; `contentRects` uses their bounding boxes, and `cutOf` includes them in partial/whole clips. Thus an intentionally oversized photograph cropped by an `overflow:hidden` frame fails as “partly clipped.” An `<img>` inside `<picture>` is included too. Fitting boxes using `object-fit:cover`, and CSS background images, are not directly detected as intrinsic-image crops. Source-confirmed; browser reproduction not run. | Restrict partial-cut, lost-at-width and reveal-content classification to text and controls. Do not emit a failing empty clip merely because cropped media overflows. Preserve separate document-overflow, accessibility and unscanned-frame checks. Add positive regressions for cropped `img`/`picture`/`video`, fitting `object-fit:cover` and background images, alongside negative text/control clipping cases. |
+| R21-GPT-02 | A | P2 | [visibility.mjs:452](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/visibility.mjs:452), [visibility.mjs:456](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/visibility.mjs:456), [visibility.mjs:467](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/visibility.mjs:467) | The supposed faintest-glyph measure uses `inkDelta:24`, cluster **best** pixels and `percentile:0.1`. Executed in-memory: thirty glyph clusters, one at **1.35:1** and twenty-nine at **12.24:1**, produce `min:1.35` but `ratio:12.24`; `resolveContrastIncomplete` returns **PASS**. Separately, nineteen pale glyphs whose channel difference is only 16 disappear from the mask; one high-contrast glyph again produces PASS. Ordinary captions crossing a light patch of a photograph are affected. Full-browser gate reproduction UNVERIFIED. | Derive glyph coverage independently of the foreground/background contrast threshold. Require AA for every measured glyph’s relevant core/local background; do not discard a failing minority through a percentile or let one strong portion excuse a connected word. Keep uncertain coverage INCOMPLETE. Add regressions for one failing glyph among thirty, sub-24-delta pale glyphs beside stronger glyphs, and connected text crossing light/dark background regions. |
+| R21-GPT-03 | A | P2 | [width-screen.mjs:72](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:72), [width-screen.mjs:245](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:245) | Reveal resolution checks only `shownAt1440.includes(p.path)`. The captured text is ignored. An ordinary separately authored expanded accordion page that introduces a wrapper changes the answer’s path and is wrongly blocked. Conversely, an unrelated paragraph occupying the former path can “reveal” an answer omitted from that state. Executed in-memory: the unrelated-path match returns `unresolved:[]`, `pass:true`, `revealedBy:['expanded']`. Browser/full-gate behavior UNVERIFIED. | Match revealed content using stable declared component/copy-slot identity plus actual normalized content; use suitable semantic identity for controls. Treat DOM paths as locators within one rendering. Add regressions for the same answer under changed wrappers, different content at the same path, and multiple identical-looking controls. |
+| R21-GPT-04 | A | P2 | [width-screen.mjs:44](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:44), [width-screen.mjs:225](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/width-screen.mjs:225), [design-quality.md:23](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/references/design-quality.md:23) | The documented rule requires “any text or control shown at 1440” to remain shown/reachable at every width. However, the cross-width loop examines only `r.clipped`; `display:none` content is excluded by `shown`, and missing content identities are never compared. A media query accidentally hiding the only Submit control at 320 therefore escapes this rule. Executed with read-only stub measurements: a control present at 1440 and absent at 320, with no overflow, returns overall **PASS**. Browser/full-gate reproduction UNVERIFIED. | Retain and compare text/control identities at every width against the 1440 baseline. Fail disappearance without an equivalent reachable representation, including `display:none` and `visibility:hidden`. Add browser regressions for an accidentally hidden action and paragraph, plus a valid equivalent responsive representation. Keep 320 as desktop accessibility reflow evidence. |
+| R21-GPT-05 | A | P2 | [integrity.mjs:273](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:273), [integrity.mjs:275](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:275) | `"canon(strip(jsOff.content)) === canon(strip(reduced.content))"` requires every default-state item to survive in the scripted state. An ordinary Settings tab replacing Profile with Notifications is blocked despite approved, correctly placed copy for both panels. Executed with identical valid vectors and a shared H1: Notifications’ permitted slot/H2 are removed, but the entire Profile baseline remains; result **INCOMPLETE**, `content/js-off`. This overextends R13 **N14** beyond shared-content equivalence. Browser/full-state reproduction UNVERIFIED. | Pass default/current placement ownership into the comparison. Compare shared slots and their owned headings/controls exactly; account separately for approved content exclusive to either state. Continue independently auditing the default rendering. Add a full-state replacement-tab regression that passes, retaining negatives for changed shared copy, missing required content and unapproved additions. |
+| R21-GPT-06 | A | P3 | [visibility.mjs:246](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/visibility.mjs:246), [visibility.mjs:510](/workspace/panel-r21/fannan/release/tools/visibility.mjs:510) | Fingerprints remain individual text-node strings. Script changing `<p>Static state text</p>` into `<p>Static <span>state</span> text</p>` changes the fingerprint boundaries without changing the rendered copy. Executed with those records: `valid:true`, `rendersWithoutScript:false`, `onlyScripted:3`. This is the remaining inline-wrapping variant of R20-GPT-04; its unusual harmful combination retains P3. | Compare normalized text/token streams independently of inline splitting/merging, preserving occurrence counts and semantic or slot boundaries. Add split-wrapper and merged-wrapper regressions. |
