## R21 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 21)

Chrome 155 headless only, 1440 × 900, device scale one. One reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar; Fadel's R21 tiebreaks.

- **Media crops (R21-MIMAR-01):** the clipping rule covers text and controls only; a box whose cut set is empty or holds only img, svg, video, canvas or decoration is recorded in `mediaCrops` and does not fail. Executed: an image cropped by its frame (LTR and RTL), an image centred in a `picture`, a hover zoom, a round avatar, a cropped video, a decorative SVG and a blob bleeding out of a section, `object-fit`, a background image; a caption and a button inside a cropped image frame and a marquee still fail. UNTESTED: `clip-path` and mask crops (not a clip box at all), iframe/object/embed crops (still treated as content), canvas crops with drawn text (the text is pixels, not checked), text drawn by `::before`/`::after` (not a content element).
- **Unrendered content (R21-MIMAR-02):** `checkVisibility()` (with display:contents boxes judged by their nearest boxed ancestor) decides whether content is on screen; closed `<details>`, `display:none`, `content-visibility: hidden` and closed popovers are not measured. In right-to-left pages content past the right (start) edge is now off-screen too (`offscreenLeft` with `side: 'right'`). Executed: a details mobile menu at 320 (RTL and LTR, the real site in both languages), an open menu whose panel is cut. UNTESTED: `content-visibility: auto` far below the fold (rendered, measured), `hidden="until-found"`, vertical writing modes.
- **Content lost at a width (R21-GPT-04):** each width's shown text and control names (normalised text, or aria-label / label / button text / placeholder / title / input value) are compared with the 1440 set; a loss fails unless the same text or name is shown at that width in the same state or in a declared state (`reachableIn`). Executed: a Subscribe button and terms line hidden at 320, a desktop nav moved into a details menu with and without a declared `menu-open` state, a menu state with different link text, an icon-only button keeping its name. UNTESTED: a control renamed at 320 (a different accessible name for the same function fails: reword or declare), text replaced by an image of the same words, names computed from `aria-labelledby`, content that only moves into a scroller at 320.
- **Read-more clamp:** a partial cut by `line-clamp` or `text-overflow: ellipsis` is `truncated` and passes only when a declared state shows the full text at that width. UNTESTED: clamps on an ancestor of the text element other than the clip box, ellipsis in vertical writing modes.
- **Faintest-text measure (R21-GPT-02):** four clipped screenshots per element (painted, transparent text, black text, white text); glyph-core pixels (coverage at least 75%), text colour recovered per pixel, graded against its own background; median per cluster, minimum over clusters; punctuation-size clusters (under 12 core pixels) on a solid background are dropped only while larger clusters remain. Executed: white caption over a dark photo with a #c8c8c8 or #e8e8e8 patch under one word (blocked through the full gate with a citing PASS review), the same without the patch, a scrim hero, small grey text over a light gradient. UNTESTED: `background-clip:text`, `mix-blend-mode`, animated backgrounds changing between the four shots, colour emoji and icon fonts (no coverage difference: they fall out of the mask), text-shadow halos (excluded from all four shots; the shadow's help is not credited), shadow-root text colours.
- **Slot replacement (R21-GPT-05):** a default slot that a valid script-only state no longer shows is dropped from the default JavaScript-off baseline only when the copy deck does not place it in that state; new content passes only as approved slots placed in the state and absent from the baseline. UNTESTED: replacements inside shadow roots, a slot replaced by the same slot id with new text (fails by design: shared copy changed).
- **Token streams (R21-GPT-06, P3) and text matching for reveals (R21-GPT-03, P3):** the requiresScript claim compares counted lower-case word tokens; reveals, truncations and losses match by print. UNTESTED: scripts in languages without spaces between words (Arabic and Latin are tokenised by spaces and punctuation), the same short string shown in several places (a print shown anywhere counts as shown).

## R20 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 20)

Chrome 155 headless only, 1440 × 900, device scale one. One reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar.

- **Clipping rule (R20-GPT-01, R20-MIMAR-01; Mi'mar's tiebreak):** each hidden/clip box reports the content elements it cuts wholly or partly (composed paths); content shown at 1440 and cut at another width fails, partial cuts fail, and wholly cut content passes only when another declared state of the same screen and language shows it at 1440 (DEFERRED in wireframes). Executed: bare-text and partly cut accordions, middle-slide carousels (LTR and RTL), a card with its last paragraph below the edge, a table and a nav cut at 320 (LTR and RTL). UNTESTED: content revealed only at a width other than 1440, vertical writing modes, content cut by `clip-path` or masks (not a clip box), reveal states declared for one language only, very large pages (the classification walks every content element per clip box). Known and unchanged: images cropped by an `overflow:hidden` frame count as partly clipped content (the built Arabic page has one, flagged by the R19 code as well).
- **Faintest-text measure (R20-GPT-03):** two clipped screenshots per element (painted, and text made transparent); glyph clusters of at least 25 pixels; the 10th percentile of cluster best-pixel contrast against the pixel underneath. UNTESTED: text with `background-clip:text`, text under `mix-blend-mode`, animated backgrounds that change between the two shots, text smaller than about 10 px (clusters below 25 pixels make it INCOMPLETE), elements taller than the viewport (only the part in view is measured), shadow-root text with its own colour rules (the transparent override does not pierce shadow roots).
- **Script-only baseline (R20-GPT-05):** for a valid `requiresScript` claim the JavaScript-off baseline is the default state's JavaScript-off rendering, and added content is removed only for approved slots placed in the state. UNTESTED: a screen without a default rendering in that language (the state keeps its own comparison), slots nested in shadow roots, vector differences that only the dialog causes (counted against the default page).
- **requiresScript fingerprints (R20-GPT-04, P3):** compared by normalized text (first 60 characters, counted). UNTESTED: a script-only state that repeats the default page's exact strings only.
- **Truncation fade (R20-GPT-02, P3):** the label needs overflowing text and a fade at the cut edge that leaves the opposite edge uncovered. UNTESTED: inline-axis fades in vertical writing modes, fades drawn by a child element instead of a pseudo-element.
- **Screen type (R20-GPT-06):** `screens[].type` is `marketing`, `landing` or `functional`; `generic-hero` is required for marketing and landing screens only. The type itself is the author's declaration and is not checked against the page.

## R19 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 19)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only, at 1440 × 900 and device scale one. Panel round 19 had one reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.

- **Width screen, hidden content (R19-GPT-01):** content a collapsed box (no inner width or height) hides, and content wholly beyond the inline-end or block-end edge of a box that cannot scroll, is not a clip; content pushed wholly past the start edge and displayed content cut partly still fail. Executed: max-height:0 accordion, LTR and RTL carousel tracks, a partly cut slide, text pushed past the start edge, the R12/R13 width suites. UNTESTED: vertical writing modes, carousels that place inactive slides before the active one (they fail as a start-edge clip), clip-path and contain:paint clippers.
- **Hidden layers (R19-GPT-02, R19-GPT-03 P3):** positioned `::before`/`::after` that paint (on the text's element or an ancestor) and positioned `pointer-events:none` layers that paint are possible covers, graded by pixels at 3:1; negative z-index layers are skipped; a gradient pseudo-element on a clipping ancestor is a truncation fade and the lines under it are not displayed; an SVG is a translucent cover. Executed: stuck and script-removed veils (both kinds), a 70% veil, a read-more fade, a decorative SVG wave, link underlines and accent bars as pseudo-elements, a z-index -1 scrim, a sticky table header, the R18 and R19 honest sets, the real built site. UNTESTED: pseudo-elements positioned with percentages, calc() or transforms (the box is taken from px offsets, else the owner's box), nested pseudo-element stacking, masks and clip-path on the layer, a pointer-events:none layer inside a closed shadow root, an opaque SVG drawn over text (now graded by pixels rather than obscured).
- **Inner scrollports (R19-GPT-04):** after each document pass the end of every visible scrollable element is visited and new content triggers another pass (bounded as before). UNTESTED: nested scrollports whose end only appears after the outer one scrolls, horizontal lazy lists in RTL, IntersectionObservers with rootMargin far outside the scrollport.
- **Colour-contrast incomplete resolver (R19-MIMAR-01; Fadel's tiebreak):** resolved only for an element the backstop measured, every line uncovered, at 4.5:1 (3:1 large) in both renderings, with a PASS `wcag-review` record citing the screenshot. The measure is the 90th-percentile ink ratio of each line (the lowest line counts), not a per-glyph minimum. UNTESTED: axe targets inside shadow roots or frames (not resolved, stay blocking), elements whose text is in several child elements (each needs its own measurement), and a declared state opened by script: its JavaScript-off rendering cannot show the dialog, so a colour-contrast incomplete on dialog text stays blocking (seen in the fixture run; a decision for Fadel). Dark text over a photo that CSS resolves against the page background is still passed by the backstop when its peak is at least 1.5:1 (axe's incomplete keeps it blocked).
- **Script-only states (R19b; Mi'mar's tiebreak):** a non-default state declared `requiresScript: true` with its `trigger` resolves a colour-contrast incomplete on the scripted rendering alone; the claim is false (integrity mismatch) when every element the scripted rendering shows is also shown with JavaScript off. UNTESTED: a script-only state whose JavaScript-off rendering shows the same elements with different text (the claim is then refused as false), and whether the recorded trigger really opens the state (it is recorded, not executed).
- **Top layer on declared states (R19-MIMAR-02; Fadel's tiebreak):** on a state other than `default`, page text outside an open `:modal` dialog (or a shown `aria-modal="true"` element) is counted as not displayed, page text an open popover covers is not graded, the dialog's and popover's own text are graded; a non-modal open dialog keeps covered text graded (obscured). UNTESTED: nested modals, `inert` set by script without a modal, fullscreen elements, customisable select pickers and other UA top-layer surfaces, aria-modal elements that do not cover the page.
- **Copy deck (R19-GPT-05/06 P3):** an `aria-labelledby` name with a hidden or undisplayed reference is an accessible name to approve; an approved `ariaLabel` must appear in its cited source. UNTESTED: `aria-labelledby` across shadow roots, `aria-description`, names from `<label>` elements that are hidden.

## R18 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 18)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only, at 1440 × 900 and device scale one. Panel round 18 had one reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.

- **Backstop role (R18-MIMAR-02, R18-GPT-04; Fadel's tiebreak):** pixels decide visibility, not AA. Where the CSS pass resolves the colours, pixels fail a line only when its strongest ink pixel is under 1.5:1 or it has fewer than three ink pixels; where it does not (background images, filters, blends, translucent covers), the 90th-percentile ink must reach 3:1. Only opaque covers (replaced elements, background colours at 90% or more opacity) obscure. Executed: Lato, Inter and Inter Tight at weights 100-400, 12-48 px, in #1a1a1a, #595959 and #767676 (180 combinations, 0 failures), a 3% white layer, the honest-pattern set below. UNTESTED: other fonts, hinting and device scale 2; text over photographs where the CSS pass is unknown and the photo is pale (graded at 3:1 by pixels, so a thin weight there can still fail); a cover between 3% and 90% opacity is graded by pixels at 3:1; only the 3% layer and the gradient fade were executed.
- **Lines from text ranges (R18-GPT-03/07):** each text node's word ranges are grouped into line boxes; the middle 60% of each line box is sampled. UNTESTED: vertical writing modes, ruby, text with negative letter spacing or overlapping lines (line-height under 1), pseudo-element text, SVG text, text nodes longer than 4,000 words (the rest is not grouped).
- **Clipped text (R18-MIMAR-01, R18-GPT-05):** text clipped to nothing by an ancestor that cannot be scrolled is not displayed (`textHidden`); text outside a scrollable ancestor's scrollport is scrolled into view (vertical and horizontal), and every scrolled ancestor is restored afterwards. Executed: carousel with and without autoplay, max-height accordion, script-opened accordion (JavaScript-off mismatch), app shell, horizontal tab strip. UNTESTED: `overflow: hidden` panels that script scrolls (treated as not scrollable, so their other text is hidden); `contain: paint` and `clip-path` on an ancestor as clippers (not used for hiding decisions; clip-path is caught by pixels); scroll snapping and scroll-driven animations that react to inner scrolling; nested scrollers more than two deep; text hidden this way in every rendering and in every declared state is never graded (that is the intended scope: declared states grade it).
- **Coverage (R18-GPT-06):** target-directed scan, at most 300 steps and four passes; early stop or growth after the last pass is INCOMPLETE. Executed: a 40,000 px page, an IntersectionObserver footer, an endless list (INCOMPLETE at a 25-step bound), the real built site (12 and 8 steps). UNTESTED: virtualised lists that remove earlier rows (targets no longer in the document are not graded), pages where every step adds content (they stop at the bound; estimated under a minute per rendering from the 25-step run), content that appears only after a timer with page scripts on and no scrolling.
- **Copy deck (R18-GPT-01, R18-GPT-02 P3):** a slot's optional `ariaLabel` (or a variant's) approves the accessible name separately; a name identical to the displayed value counts once; option labels are screened. UNTESTED: `aria-labelledby` names (not matched to the deck), `aria-description`, accessible names on display:contents elements.

## R17 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 17)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only, at 1440 × 900 and device scale one. Panel round 17 had one reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.

- **Rendered-visibility backstop (R17-MIMAR-01/02, R17-GPT-02):** hit test plus screenshot-pixel contrast in both renderings (method in `references/design-quality.md`, code in `tools/visibility.mjs`). Executed: clip-path, `scale(.02)`, a white full-viewport preloader, `::placeholder` opacity, `-webkit-text-fill-color` and a gradient overlay, each removed by script, are a JavaScript-off mismatch in Chrome and in full pre-handoff runs; a permanent fade overlay, a permanent faint fill and text clipped to nothing fail or are INCOMPLETE; a long healthy page (sticky header, grey text on light bands, icon button, controls, visually hidden label, dark footer) and normal animations (load fade-in, IntersectionObserver scroll reveal with a `noscript` fallback, an infinite spinner, a requestAnimationFrame tween) pass with JavaScript on and off, as do a skip link above or left of the page, a closed `<details>` menu, a `display:none` menu, a disabled button, a thin grey separator glyph and content that grows the page. Healthy-page survey outside the fixture (box only, external requests blocked): a built bilingual company site (English and Arabic, GSAP scroll reveals, served locally) showed false positives with the first version (closed menu, skip link, script tweens, a growing page); after the fixes it has none, with JavaScript on or off. Twenty draft section pages showed only text the CSS pass also fails (light grey labels, faded placeholders) after a thin-glyph and disabled-control fix. UNTESTED: text over photographs, video or canvas (the modal background can be a photo colour); very thin or tiny fonts near the 3:1 floor (antialiasing lowers the measured ink); pseudo-element and SVG text (not targets); text inside closed shadow roots, frames, `<details>` and open select lists; horizontally scrolled containers (text outside the scrollport is clipped to nothing, INCOMPLETE); continuous script motion (an autoplaying carousel) ends each band's settle at the 2 s bound and is measured mid-motion (counted in `unsettledBands`); scroll-linked (scrubbed) reveals are measured at the band's scroll position; pages taller than about 20 viewports (run time grows by one screenshot per half viewport); other viewports and device scales. A covering element with `pointer-events: none` is not in the hit-test stack; only the pixels catch it.
- **Hiding by opacity alone:** text left rendered with `opacity: 0` (a closed menu, an inactive tab) is unreadable to the backstop and fails with JavaScript on. Use `hidden`, `display: none` or `visibility: hidden` for inactive content.
- **Controls (R17-GPT-01):** a control's displayed value (button-type input value, or the browser's default label for submit and reset without one) is compared separately from its accessible name. UNTESTED: file-selector and date-picker labels, `<button>` elements whose label is CSS generated content.
- **Native copy (R17-GPT-03):** button-type input values, placeholders, every option label of a shown select, datalist options, `aria-label`, image `alt` and `title` are screened for placeholders and filler; values, placeholders, option labels and `aria-label` must sit in a copy slot whose deck text contains them. Typed or fixture values of text fields are user data and are not matched. UNTESTED: `aria-description`, `aria-placeholder`, live-region text and text that script writes after load into native attributes only.
- **Filter decision:** unchanged and fail-closed: unresolved compositing on text is INCOMPLETE in either rendering; the pixel-measured exception is ENH backlog, not built.

## R16 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 16)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only. Panel round 16 had one reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.

- **Compositing (R16-GPT-01):** `filter: opacity()` is composited like opacity; identity filters are ignored; any other filter function, a blend mode, a backdrop filter or a mask anywhere on the text's composed ancestor chain makes that text unknown (`contrastEffects`), and the cross-check is INCOMPLETE in either rendering. Consequence: a page that keeps such an effect on text cannot pass the integrity cross-check, by design. UNTESTED: effects on pseudo-elements or SVG text; `filter` values set through `url()` to an SVG filter that is in fact an identity (counted unknown); text painted inside a canvas.
- **Native controls (R16-GPT-02):** values, placeholders (with the `::placeholder` colour), button-type input labels and a select's chosen option are contrast-checked; controls, links, images and elements with a role or ARIA label are compared with their accessible name and displayed value. The accessible name is an approximation of the specification (aria-labelledby, aria-label, label elements, value, alt, own text, title, placeholder), not the full algorithm. UNTESTED: `::file-selector-button`, date and time pickers, autofill colours, `<option>` lists while open, names from CSS generated content. As before, an unexplained JavaScript-off content difference records a content mismatch and the cross-check status is INCOMPLETE (R13 N14).
- **Wireframe coverage (R16-GPT-03):** the wireframe phase requires each screen's page to exist, an applicable default rendering per declared language, manual records per screen and language, and renders each declared screen/language with phase-appropriate checks (no frame hash, type, accent, spacing or placeholder thresholds yet). Links inside the pages (navigation between screens) are not followed.
- **Component inventory (R16-GPT-04):** the contract enforces one shared definition per component, references by id, declared variants and states, and equality of any repeated specification field; the critic records a component comparison covering every screen. Whether two instances that do not repeat a field are visually consistent is a reviewer judgment (`component-consistency`), not machine-checked.

## R15 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 15)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only. Panel round 15 had one reviewer (GPT); B4 was found by Mi'mar alone. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.

- **Width screen (A1):** an `overflow-y: auto`/`scroll` ancestor holds lower text only when its scrollport ends inside the visible viewport (and above every clipping ancestor) and its scroll range reaches the text. UNTESTED: scrollers moved by transforms, scroll-snap or scroll-driven animation; a scroller whose visible part is cut by a sibling overlay rather than an ancestor clip.
- **Package (A2):** JSON files (by suffix, or text starting with `{` or `[`) are parsed and every key is screened with `credential_key()` (any case or separator, camelCase too), 8+ character string values; the regex stays for other text and now names access/refresh tokens and secret/access keys case-insensitively. Known limit: credentials in YAML, TOML or `.env`-style text under keys the regex does not name; JSON with comments (not parseable) falls back to the regex only.
- **Contrast (A3):** CSS `opacity` on the text and its composed ancestors is composited (premultiplied groups); a `mix-blend-mode` on the chain is counted unknown. UNTESTED: `filter: opacity()`/`brightness()`, opacity set through the Web Animations API mid-animation, `mask`, and colour-mix or relative colours that compute to non-`rgb()` strings (counted unknown, not measured).
- **Designer process (B1-B4):** the complete wireframe gate now runs inside Step 5 after the task and findability tests; column counts are unitless; `feedback-log`, `emphasis-order`, `type-measure`, `colour-roles` and `grid-per-width` are manual IDs (the last four PASS or DEFERRED in the wireframe phase); every critic check names a rubric row and the final round needs a passing check per row. The contract checks that the records exist with evidence; whether the feedback log, emphasis check, type measure, colour matrix, grid and critic judgments are good is a reviewer judgment, not machine-checked. No real project was run through the new Step 5 order.

## R14 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 14)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only. Panel round 14 had one reviewer (GPT) and no cross-check; Mi'mar acted as the second Part B reviewer. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.

- **Content and contrast (R14-GPT-01/02):** copy slots and headings count as rendered when their text ranges have area (`display: contents`, zero-size boxes); contrast walks open shadow roots and resolves backgrounds through slots and hosts. UNTESTED: text inside closed shadow roots (fails as an unscanned scope in the width screen, not in the contrast diagnostic); backgrounds painted by a slotted element's light-DOM ancestors that the slot's own composed chain does not include.
- **Width screen (R14-GPT-03/04):** closed shadow roots are counted at each width after a bounded settle (two animation frames or 250 ms); a viewport that cannot scroll vertically (html, or a propagated body, with `overflow: hidden`/`clip`) fails text and media below its bottom edge unless an inner scroller holds them. UNTESTED: a closed root created later than the settle; `position: sticky` content; horizontal reach on a hidden viewport beyond the existing overflow check.
- **Reduced motion (R14-GPT-05):** the snapshot covers the composed tree with composed-path keys, on the page and every state (executed fixture runs). UNTESTED: motion inside closed shadow roots or frames; motion that only starts after the 700 ms window.
- **Package (R14-GPT-06):** credential keys anywhere in `tokens.json` (every dict and list) are refused, and the content screen refuses JSON credential keys with real-looking values (8+ characters). Known limit: credentials under keys the list does not name, or values shorter than 8 characters.
- **Designer process (R14-GPT-07 to 11, R14-MIMAR-01 to 05):** the text and manual-check IDs are present and enforced by tests and the package build; whether a real project's ledger, navigation model, task tests, state and form specifications, feedback log, emphasis check, type measure, colour matrix and per-width grid are good is a reviewer judgment, not machine-checked. No real project was run through them.

## R13 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 13)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md` (honest but possibly sloppy authors; fail closed on what cannot be measured; deliberate obfuscation is a known limit, ENH in future rounds).

- **Frames (N04, N05, N21):** `iframe`, `frame`, `object`, `embed`, `fencedframe` and `portal` are nested scopes. Same-origin frames are partially inspected, for glass and width only, and every one of them fails the final handoff (DEFERRED in wireframes); there are no frame exceptions (q1). UNTESTED: no test renders a `fencedframe` or `portal`; only their presence in the selectors is checked.
- **Width screen (N01-N03, N15, N16):** body overflow that propagates to the viewport, zero-size and `display: contents` wrappers, shadow text clipped by its host, keyboard reach across a table and closed shadow roots (counted through CDP, reported as unscanned) were each reproduced and fixed. UNTESTED: a closed shadow root inside a frame; CDP counting when DevTools domains are unavailable is reported as unscanned, not exercised.
- **Stylesheets (N07):** `data:` and `blob:` stylesheets are refused; a stylesheet the probe cannot read and the checker did not serve fails. UNTESTED: `@import` chains deeper than one level in shadow roots.
- **Known limits, raw glass (N08/N09):** `\xNN`, `\uNNNN` and `\u{...}` escapes are decoded and the raw and comment-stripped text are both matched. Not covered (obfuscation, out of the threat model): string concatenation (`'backdrop-' + 'filter'`), `String.fromCharCode`, `atob`, computed property names, template literals assembled at run time, and CSS built from variables in script. The computed-style check and the JavaScript-off pass remain the defences.
- **Known limits, reduced motion (N17, N18):** the native `requestAnimationFrame` is bound at install, and `Function.prototype.call`/`apply`/`bind` and `Reflect.apply` are in the native-function check; page and states share one routine. Not covered: a page that hides patches from `Function.prototype.toString` (heuristic; the between-world comparison remains), rAF called from an `about:blank` child frame created after the init script, and animation started by timers after the 700 ms window.
- **Integrity (N11-N14, N19):** the vector now carries every hard-fail input (accent ratios, filler, rule of three, frames, unscanned stylesheets and scopes, per-width maps, contrast unknown/coverage); content compares slot and heading text; a content waiver is INCOMPLETE, never PASS; the native-function check has no default. UNTESTED: JavaScript-off equivalence for content inserted by CSS (`content:` on pseudo-elements).
- **Shadow DOM (N20):** spacing, design counters, placeholders, h1 and the copy walker use the composed tree including open shadow roots. UNTESTED: slotted light-DOM content assigned to named slots in nested shadow trees.
- **Package (N10, q2):** a credential word anywhere in a path part is refused (except three reviewed tool, test and evidence names); `tokens.json` passes only where the `handoff.json` beside it declares that path and hash and the content is design tokens; a stdlib content screen refuses obvious secrets (private-key blocks, cloud and chat tokens, OAuth secret values) in every packaged or hashed file. Known limit: secrets in formats the screen does not know, and binary files.

## R12 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, panel round 12)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only.

- **Accent area and stray colours (M19, closed):** the accent check binds the declared variable to the approved token only. Accent area and coverage are approximate (a DOM background-area proxy) and are decided by screenshots and the manual `accent-area` and `palette` reviews (panel A). A page that paints large areas in another, unapproved colour is NOT failed automatically. UNTESTED by design.
- **Frames (M03):** any frame (same-origin, `data:`, sandboxed or cross-origin) fails the final handoff and is recorded as DEFERRED in wireframes, because axe and the probes run in the main frame only. The R11 line below that called such frames "blocked" was wrong: they were recorded, not gated. Frame content is still not inspected (a frame is a stop, not a scan). *(Superseded by R13 N21: frames are partially inspected, for glass and width, and every frame, object, embed or fencedframe fails the handoff.)*
- **Raw glass (M04/M05):** served HTML, JavaScript and SVG count any `backdrop-filter`/`-webkit-backdrop-filter` mention not followed by `: none`, and the identifiers `backdropFilter`/`webkitBackdropFilter`; CSS escapes are resolved first; ordinary CSSOM sheets are read in the page. UNTESTED: glass built from strings at run time (`'backdrop' + 'Filter'`), and sheets whose rules the page cannot read (left to the served-file scan).
- **Integrity (M06-M08, M17):** the full hard-fail vector (glass, h1, placeholders, centred, type sizes, hero gradient, purple-blue, icon rows, accent, spacing off-scale, overflow, clipped, offscreen-left, unreachable, scrolled text, unmeasured, reflow, contrast) is compared page world vs probe world and with JavaScript off, on the positional page and on every declared state. Contrast is a custom diagnostic (text vs resolved solid background, 4.5:1 / 3:1), not axe: axe cannot run with JavaScript off. JavaScript-off content (visible copy slots, h1 count, lang, dir) must match or the cross-check is INCOMPLETE. UNTESTED: text over images or gradients in the contrast diagnostic (counted as unknown, not failed); the native-function check stays a heuristic.
- **320 px reflow (M01, M02, M09-M11, M14):** scrollers are measured with their own text, open shadow roots and same-origin frames; content outside a scroller's reachable range is `unreachable` at every width; keyboard use means an explicit `tabindex >= 0` scroller or usable targets that step across the whole extent; candidates and their exceptions are scoped to screen/state/lang. UNTESTED: closed shadow roots, `overflow: overlay`, scroll snapping, and whether a resolved candidate genuinely needs 2D layout (the reviewer's decision). *(Superseded in part by R13 N21: same-origin frames are partially inspected and fail the handoff anyway.)*
- **Reduced motion (M13):** the rAF counter is private and the wrapper non-writable; a non-finite or decreasing reading counts as a loop. UNTESTED: animation driven by timers or CSS that a page starts after the 700 ms window.
- **Spacing (M15, M20):** `html` and `body` margins are screened; every `data-fannan-spacing-exception` needs a scoped handoff `spacingExceptions` entry naming the approver. UNTESTED: exceptions on pseudo-elements.
- **Package (M12):** environment files (`.env*`), editor locks (`.#*`), credential folders (`.ssh`, `.gnupg`, `.aws`) and credential names (`credentials`, `secrets`, `service-account`, `token`, `.npmrc`, `.netrc`, `.pypirc`, `.git-credentials`) are refused with any suffix. Plural `tokens` stays allowed because design-token files are named `tokens.json`. UNTESTED: secrets inside ordinarily named files (names only; the secret grep is manual).

## R11 additions (Mi'mar, 18 October 2026, Asad panel round 5 and panel D1 decisions)

All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only.

- **axe tags (C1):** `wcag21a` and `wcag22a` added; a test checks the set against the pinned axe-core 4.14.0 rule tags. axe's experimental A/AA rules (`css-orientation-lock`, `p-as-heading`, `table-fake-caption`, `td-has-header`) stay off and remain manual. UNTESTED: other axe versions.
- **Accent (panel A):** bound to the approved `colors.accent`/`colors.primary` token. FAIL at handoff with the variable named; DEFERRED in wireframes. The area stays an approximate DOM proxy. UNTESTED: colour spaces beyond sRGB comparing equal after canvas normalisation.
- **Glass (S2/C6, panel D):** computed on `html`, `body`, visible elements and rendered pseudo-elements, in open shadow roots and same-origin (srcdoc) frames, plus constructed stylesheets and raw-text scans of served CSS/HTML/SVG/JS, style attributes and `<style>`. Any raw `backdrop-filter` other than `none` fails, even when the rule never applies (fail closed). NOT COVERED: closed shadow roots (unreachable from script) and cross-origin frames (blocked by the checker; listed as `unscannedFrames`). `file://` frames are cross-origin in Chrome, so their glass is caught only by the served-file text scan. A `-webkit-` alias added by a script in a constructed sheet is caught only by that text scan (Chrome drops it when parsing). Styles injected later than the probes run are UNTESTED. *(Superseded by R13 N21: frames are partially inspected and every frame fails the handoff.)*
- **320 px reflow (S3, panel B):** candidates only, recorded and resolved by `reflowExceptions`; keyboard use means `tabindex` on the scroller or a focusable child. Chrome's automatic focusable scrollers are not counted. UNTESTED: `overflow: overlay`, scrollers in shadow roots, and whether a resolved candidate genuinely needs 2D layout (that is the reviewer's decision).
- **Probe world and integrity (C3, panel C):** probes and axe run in a CDP isolated world (not a Playwright API). The page-world vs probe-world comparison, the native-function check (a heuristic: a page can hide a patch from `toString`) and the JavaScript-off pass run on the positional page only, not on every state. The JavaScript-off pass compares glass and the 320 px screen. Contrast is NOT cross-checked with JavaScript off, because axe does not complete with page scripts disabled in Chrome 155. Iframes get no isolated world of their own. Page scripts that change the DOM or CSS between the two world measurements could cause a false mismatch (UNTESTED).
- **Package (C4, panel D):** explicit suffix allowlist plus denial of `.env*`, keys, certificates, credential dotfiles, OS junk, editor files and VCS files, both in package input and among changed paths. Checked with temporary trees. UNTESTED: secrets inside ordinarily named files (only names are screened; the separate secret grep is manual).
- **Spacing (S7, panel D):** left, right and logical margins; `auto` and 0 are ignored; `data-fannan-spacing-exception` is recorded. UNTESTED: exceptions on pseudo-elements.

