    49	
    50	All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only, at 1440 × 900 and device scale one. Panel round 17 had one reviewer (GPT), cross-checked by Mi'mar. Scope follows the threat model in `FANNAN-PLAN.md`.
    51	
    52	- **Rendered-visibility backstop (R17-MIMAR-01/02, R17-GPT-02):** hit test plus screenshot-pixel contrast in both renderings (method in `references/design-quality.md`, code in `tools/visibility.mjs`). Executed: clip-path, `scale(.02)`, a white full-viewport preloader, `::placeholder` opacity, `-webkit-text-fill-color` and a gradient overlay, each removed by script, are a JavaScript-off mismatch in Chrome and in full pre-handoff runs; a permanent fade overlay, a permanent faint fill and text clipped to nothing fail or are INCOMPLETE; a long healthy page (sticky header, grey text on light bands, icon button, controls, visually hidden label, dark footer) and normal animations (load fade-in, IntersectionObserver scroll reveal with a `noscript` fallback, an infinite spinner, a requestAnimationFrame tween) pass with JavaScript on and off, as do a skip link above or left of the page, a closed `<details>` menu, a `display:none` menu, a disabled button, a thin grey separator glyph and content that grows the page. Healthy-page survey outside the fixture (box only, external requests blocked): a built bilingual company site (English and Arabic, GSAP scroll reveals, served locally) showed false positives with the first version (closed menu, skip link, script tweens, a growing page); after the fixes it has none, with JavaScript on or off. Twenty draft section pages showed only text the CSS pass also fails (light grey labels, faded placeholders) after a thin-glyph and disabled-control fix. UNTESTED: text over photographs, video or canvas (the modal background can be a photo colour); very thin or tiny fonts near the 3:1 floor (antialiasing lowers the measured ink); pseudo-element and SVG text (not targets); text inside closed shadow roots, frames, `<details>` and open select lists; horizontally scrolled containers (text outside the scrollport is clipped to nothing, INCOMPLETE); continuous script motion (an autoplaying carousel) ends each band's settle at the 2 s bound and is measured mid-motion (counted in `unsettledBands`); scroll-linked (scrubbed) reveals are measured at the band's scroll position; pages taller than about 20 viewports (run time grows by one screenshot per half viewport); other viewports and device scales. A covering element with `pointer-events: none` is not in the hit-test stack; only the pixels catch it.
    53	- **Hiding by opacity alone:** text left rendered with `opacity: 0` (a closed menu, an inactive tab) is unreadable to the backstop and fails with JavaScript on. Use `hidden`, `display: none` or `visibility: hidden` for inactive content.
    54	- **Controls (R17-GPT-01):** a control's displayed value (button-type input value, or the browser's default label for submit and reset without one) is compared separately from its accessible name. UNTESTED: file-selector and date-picker labels, `<button>` elements whose label is CSS generated content.
    55	- **Native copy (R17-GPT-03):** button-type input values, placeholders, every option label of a shown select, datalist options, `aria-label`, image `alt` and `title` are screened for placeholders and filler; values, placeholders, option labels and `aria-label` must sit in a copy slot whose deck text contains them. Typed or fixture values of text fields are user data and are not matched. UNTESTED: `aria-description`, `aria-placeholder`, live-region text and text that script writes after load into native attributes only.
    56	- **Filter decision:** unchanged and fail-closed: unresolved compositing on text is INCOMPLETE in either rendering; the pixel-measured exception is ENH backlog, not built.
